{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1229","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C1229","description":["The sodium salt of selenium.  As a trace mineral that is toxic in high doses, selenium is a cofactor for glutathione peroxidase, an anti-oxidant enzyme that neutralizes hydrogen peroxide.  Selenium may be chemoprotective for certain cancers, particularly prostate cancer.  High dietary supplementation with sodium selenate may inhibit the progression of hormone-refractory prostate cancer due, in part, to an antiangiogenesis effect. (NCI04)"],"label":"Sodium Selenate","obo_id":"NCIT:C1229","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["SODIUM SELENATE","Selenate, Sodium","Sodium Selenate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_77775","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["NSC-378348","Natriumseleniat","Selenic acid, disodium salt","Sodium selenate","Sodium selenium oxide","disodium selenate"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_77775","description":["An inorganic sodium salt having selenate as the counterion."],"label":"sodium selenate","obo_id":"CHEBI:77775","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["disodium selenate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_48843","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["NSC-347466","Na2SeO3","Natriumselenit","Sodium selenite (selenium-75)","Sodium selenite anhydrous","Sodium selenite se-75","disodium selenite","disodium selenium trioxide","selenious acid (H2SeO3) disodium salt","selenious acid disodium salt","selenious acid, disodium salt","selenious acid, sodium salt (1:2)","sodium selenite"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_48843","description":["An inorganic sodium salt composed of sodium and selenite ions in a 2:1 ratio."],"label":"disodium selenite","obo_id":"CHEBI:48843","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["disodium selenite"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C87346","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C87346","description":["An inorganic form of the trace element selenium with potential antineoplastic activity. Selenium, administered in the form of sodium selenite, is reduced to hydrogen selenide (H2Se) in the presence of glutathione (GSH) and subsequently generates superoxide radicals upon reaction with oxygen. This may inhibit the expression and activity of the transcription factor Sp1; in turn Sp1 down-regulates androgen receptor (AR) expression and blocks AR signaling. Eventually, selenium may induce apoptosis in prostate cancer cells and inhibit tumor cell proliferation."],"label":"Sodium Selenite","obo_id":"NCIT:C87346","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Disodium Selenium Trioxide","SODIUM SELENITE","Selenious Acid Disodium Salt","Selenious Acid, Sodium Salt (1:2)","Sodium Selenite"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_131361","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Na2SeO3.5H2O","Selenious acid disodium salt, pentahydrate","Sodium selenite pentahydrate","disodium selenite hydrate","sodium selenite hydrate","sodium selenite--water (1/5)"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_131361","description":["A hydrate that is the pentahydrate form of disodium selenite."],"label":"disodium selenite pentahydrate","obo_id":"CHEBI:131361","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["sodium selenite--water (1/5)"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C87347","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C87347","description":[],"label":"Sodium Selenite Pentahydate","obo_id":"NCIT:C87347","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["SODIUM SELENITE PENTAHYDRATE","Selenious Acid, Disodium Salt, Pentahydrate","Sodium Selenite Pentahydate"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C87345","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C87345","description":[],"label":"Sodium Biselenite","obo_id":"NCIT:C87345","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Hydrogen Sodium Selenium Oxide","Monosodium Selenite","SODIUM BISELENITE","Selenious Acid, Monosodium Salt","Sodium Biselenite","Sodium Hydrogen Selenite","Sodium Hydroselenite"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_77773","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["Disodium monoselenide","Na2Se","disodium selenide"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_77773","description":["An inorganic sodium salt having selenide as the counterion."],"label":"sodium selenide","obo_id":"CHEBI:77773","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["disodium selenide"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45499","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C45499","description":["Any inorganic compound containing selenium, including sodium selenite, sodium selenate, selenium sulfides, selenic acid, selenium dioxide and hydrogen selenide. Selenium is an essential component of selenoproteins that are important antioxidant enzymes."],"label":"Selenium Compound","obo_id":"NCIT:C45499","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Selenium Compound"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_9925","ontology_name":"chebi","related_synonyms":["2-Propylvaleric acid sodium salt","A-44090","ABBOTT 44090","ABBOTT-44090","Depacon","Depakene","Epilim 200","Epilim 500","Epilim chrono 200","Epilim chrono 300","Epilim chrono 500","Epilim chronosphere","Epilim iv","Epilim","Episenta","KW-6066N","Kentilim","NSC-732626","NSC-757376","Natrii valproas","Orfiril","Orlept","Selenica","Valproate sodium","Valproic acid sodium salt (1:1)","Valproic acid, sodium salt","Valproic acid, sodium","sodium 2-propylpentanoate","valproate sodium","valproic acid sodium salt"],"ontology_prefix":"CHEBI","short_form":"CHEBI_9925","description":["The sodium salt of valproic acid."],"label":"sodium valproate","obo_id":"CHEBI:9925","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["sodium 2-propylpentanoate"]}],"numFound":10,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["CHEBI","5","NCIT","5"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","10"],"ontologyId":["dron","15","snomed","6","mesh","6","chebi","5","ncit","5","micro","4","slm","4","agro","2","mco","2","oba","1","omit","1","pride","1","hp","1","efo","1","upheno","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chebi.owl","5","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","5"],"isObsolete":["false","10"],"type":["class","10"]}}}